WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.634
For Secretary Stoltenberg.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.669
What impact does

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.170
Naito expect the Wagner

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.972
events to have on the battlefield

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.273
in Ukraine?

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.809
And German Minister Pistorius

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.011
I was just ask

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.179
why did Germany change its decision

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.048
about having permanent troops

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.149
based in Lithuania?

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:16.983
Was this at all

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.218
tied to the Faulkner

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.252
events over the weekend,

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:21.154
or was this in motion already before?

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.022
Thank you.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.692
I think what we're seeing in Russia

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:26.960
over the last days

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:27.694
demonstrates

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.096
the fragility of the German regime

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.898
and of course of this

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:33.900
social weakness of the regime

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.468
when there are

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.937
so lots of German regimes.

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.739
Oh, sorry, the Russian

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.341
I'm sorry,

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.543
they're quite stable at the moment.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:46.112
So we see that the weakness of the

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.480
of the rest of the team

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.215
and it also demonstrates

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:53.186
how how difficult and dangerous this for

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:54.788
President Putin

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:57.157
to be reliant on mercenaries

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.659
that have actually turned against him.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.362
And it also demonstrates that

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:04.497
it is hard

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.598
to predict exactly

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:06.633
what will now happen

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.635
in the next days and weeks.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:11.071
But we should not make the mistakes

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.606
that we are underestimating the Russians.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.509
So we need to continue to provide

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.645
support to Ukraine

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:19.512
And that's exactly what,

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:22.382
Nathan, that our allies are doing with

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.451
military support,

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.953
but also support for the long term

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.523
and that's in a way

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.792
what we can say today about the effects

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.128
on the battlefield in Ukraine.

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:37.564
That's NATO's need to react in any way

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.666
on the recent developments in Russia.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:42.035
But President Nauseda, for example,

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:45.872
suggested yesterday to strengthen

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.942
the eastern flank of NATO Right now,

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.477
if the volcano troops

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:52.345
will settle in Belarus,

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.613
is that an option

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.181
from your point of view?

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.749
Or are there any consequences

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.651
for the NATO-Russia founding act?

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.655
And my second question to you would be

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.725
what message goes out from the

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:06.860
permanent deployment

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:07.827
of the German brigade

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.729
that was announced by Minister

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.197
Pistorius today?

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.299
What message goes out to Mr.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.200
Putin and Mr.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.003
Lukashenko from the deployment

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.905
and the Sunosi question

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:22.142
on the brigade to the.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.145
The condition is that Lithuania

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.547
builds the infrastructure

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:28.748
for the brigade.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.917
And by when will that be finished?

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.921
Let me start by saying that we,

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.256
of course, very much

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:38.391
welcome the German leadership,

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.928
which has been demonstrated

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.496
throughout actually a long time.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.899
But it's very much

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:49.502
enhanced by the German announcement today

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.539
because Germany led the battle group.

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:56.609
But also more German troops deployed here

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.712
shows a strong German commitment

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.915
to our collective defense,

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.516
to our shared security.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:07.187
And it's part of the adaptation of NATO's

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.322
which has taken place since 2014

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.791
with higher readiness of forces,

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.860
but also with more

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.729
deployments of combat troops

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.765
in the eastern part of the lines

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.667
including the battlegroups.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:21.501
And one of them is

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:24.437
that German led group here in Lithuania.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.805
So this demonstrates

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:26.973
German leadership,

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.141
German commitment

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.876
to our trans-Atlantic bond.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.010
And it also demonstrates

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.278
the value of

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.280
a multilateral NATO commitment

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.150
to a country like Lithuania.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.086
It sends of course a message

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.087
our presence here

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.088
and also the exercise

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:44.991
we just watched of NATO's readiness

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.360
and the NATO's capability

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.996
to defend every inch of NATO's territory.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.165
And the reason we do that is,

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.900
of course, not to provoke a conflict,

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.802
but it is to prevent the conflict,

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:58.304
because credible deterrence

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.073
is about preventing war.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.341
It's about preventing conflict

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.175
is it's about preventing

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.544
an attack and preserving peace.

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.479
And this is not only about

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.514
the forward presence, which is important,

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.616
but it's also about

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.485
pre-positioned equipment,

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:15.788
supplies, high readiness and exercises.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.790
So it's all of this together,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.826
but also by significant

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.828
air and naval power

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:22.695
and that also fits

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.097
into the issue of air defense,

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:24.797
I think,

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.132
of course, Land-based

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:28.201
air defense systems are important,

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.436
but we have to understand that

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.004
when we now

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:32.839
have this rotational model in place

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.340
for air defense,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.009
which can make it easier for us

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.043
to switch from air

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.611
policing to air defense,

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.179
air forces is also part of air

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:43.116
defense and naval forces can also provide

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:44.317
significant air

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:45.184
defense capabilities

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.620
on very short notice.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.454
So

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.024
this is the general announcement.

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:53.526
This is welcomed under, under,

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:55.495
and it's part of a pattern

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.030
big adaptation of NATO,

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.097
and that has taken place

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.866
over several years.

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:00.867
One more thing about this

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:01.567
is that

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.136
we will also make important decisions

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:06.472
at the Vilnius and summit on

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:09.375
on the new force structure, the new

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.311
force model, and also

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:13.713
with plans that will

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.448
dedicate specific forces

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:17.750
to protect specific territories.

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:19.118
This is the first time

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.386
since of the Cold War

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:22.221
where we are going to have

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:23.356
plans linked

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:24.390
to specific forces

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:27.226
to protect specific territories.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:29.329
Then the first question also

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:33.066
yeah.

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.601
Well, first of all,

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:38.004
I think it's a bit early to say exactly,

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:40.873
because I things might still evolve.

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:43.409
Second, we are, of course,

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.111
monitoring very closely

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:47.847
and and we are able to react quickly

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.816
if there is a need at the same time,

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:52.352
I think it is important to remind

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.021
you all that this is about internal

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:58.791
Russian matters and and therefore

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:00.093
what NATO's focused on

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:02.662
is to support Ukraine.

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:03.563
It demonstrates

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:06.899
the fragility of the Russian team,

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:10.269
but it's not for NATO's in intervene

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:12.138
in those issues.

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:14.040
That's a Russian matter.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:15.475
What matters for NATO

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:17.877
is to not be intimidated, not be

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:19.912
prevented from

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:21.180
continue to provide

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.282
unprecedented support for Ukraine

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.717
and also, of course,

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:25.852
to have the necessary

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:26.886
deterrence on defense.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:28.187
We have that already.

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:29.956
We have increased our presence

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:30.656
over the years.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:31.791
And with the German announcement

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:32.091
here, yet

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:33.159
another example of how

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:35.161
allies are increasing their presence.

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:35.561
But again,

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:36.462
it's not only about

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:37.196
presence, it's

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:37.997
also about the ability

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.832
to have early warning indications

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:42.468
and then react quickly if is a need.

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:43.503
And this exercise

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.037
demonstrates exactly that.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.273
Let's speak to Nic Robertson.

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:49.275
He's having to juggle all of this.

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:50.309
And it's so fast moving.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:51.811
And you can see that when Stoltenberg

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:52.812
is speaking,

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:53.946
the sensitivities here,

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:54.814
because they regard it

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:56.983
as an internal Russian matter

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:58.985
but they do feel obviously

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:00.420
they have to monitor

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.921
what happens in terms

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.790
of how it might affect Ukraine.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.425
And that was one of the questions

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:06.359
that was asked.

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:08.661
And I think his point was in particular,

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:11.197
don't underestimate Russia.

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.265
That's the key thing.

00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:14.000
We need to keep supporting Ukraine.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.068
And the questions were involved.

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:17.904
Will Prigozhin

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:19.705
essentially in Belarus pose

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.707
a bigger threat to NATO?

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.276
Because when he bring his forces

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:23.709
there, these

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:25.011
these are unknowns,

00:07:25.011 --> 00:07:27.713
although that seems very unlikely

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:28.781
What's interesting here

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.082
is this disposition.

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:31.651
You just put NATO's disposition

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:32.919
of additional

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:35.388
air assets on the eastern flank.

00:07:35.388 --> 00:07:37.390
And I was recently covering

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.859
the NATO's air defender exercise,

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:41.461
where it was all about

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:43.296
training different pilots

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:44.897
from different countries together.

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:46.199
But the commander,

00:07:46.199 --> 00:07:46.699
the German

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:48.468
commander in charge of that, said

00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:49.836
one of the big takeaways

00:07:49.836 --> 00:07:50.636
from watching

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:50.970
the way

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.772
Russia fights the war in Ukraine

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.674
is control of airspace.

00:07:54.674 --> 00:07:55.741
And what you heard Secretary

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.811
General Stoltenberg speak about there

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:01.581
was the importance of,

00:08:02.048 --> 00:08:02.748
again,

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:05.384
being able to control that airspace.

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:06.752
It's clear

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:08.054
that NATO

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:10.122
sees the way that the war is being

00:08:10.122 --> 00:08:11.290
fought in Ukraine

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:15.228
and is stepping up its ability to deal

00:08:15.228 --> 00:08:16.929
with an overseas spill

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:18.698
the way that Russia's fighting it

00:08:18.698 --> 00:08:20.967
with missiles, with drones.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.135
That's what these fighter aircraft

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:24.871
could this turn from policing

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:26.739
to defense of NATO's

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:28.107
would find themselves doing.

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:29.909
But yes, in the context of

00:08:29.909 --> 00:08:32.345
the Wagner situation over the weekend.

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:33.679
I don't

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:34.680
think NATO's or anyone else

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.782
is taking their eye off the ball

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:38.417
but the diplomatic message

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:40.086
from Stoltenberg,

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:41.020
the same as we've heard

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:41.854
from the State Department

00:08:41.854 --> 00:08:43.022
and from others,

00:08:43.022 --> 00:08:44.991
this shows the fragility

00:08:44.991 --> 00:08:47.159
of the Russian leadership.

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:48.561
But don't think that it's going to change

00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:49.228
anything on the ground

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:50.463
immediately in Ukraine.

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:52.932
We've had some video from Putin today.

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:54.200
We've had some video

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.801
of the defense minister

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:57.436
out there on the front lines as well.

00:08:57.436 --> 00:08:57.803
We don't know

00:08:57.803 --> 00:09:00.439
where either of them were filmed,

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:01.941
but this is how they're messaging right

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:02.408
now, isn't it,

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:04.043
that we are still in control?

00:09:04.043 --> 00:09:05.077
And, you know,

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:06.245
in terms of the defense minister,

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:07.680
very interesting because that's the guy

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.682
the because you wanted to get rid of.

00:09:09.682 --> 00:09:10.850
But they're saying he's here

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:14.020
almost saying he's still here.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:15.221
They're not saying the how long

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:16.322
is going to be around for.

00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:17.223
Yes, absolutely.

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:17.423
Look,

00:09:17.423 --> 00:09:19.992
this is the Kremlin messaging saying

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:21.394
nothing to see here, folks.

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:24.330
Move on, lifting the security,

00:09:25.231 --> 00:09:27.233
strict restriction in Moscow,

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:28.367
which was severe,

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:29.235
there was going to be

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:30.836
no going to work on Monday

00:09:30.836 --> 00:09:31.203
and there were going

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:32.572
to be no public events

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:33.973
until the beginning of July.

00:09:33.973 --> 00:09:36.208
So all of that's gone

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:37.643
it's

00:09:37.944 --> 00:09:40.980
the Kremlin is taking the attitude of

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:45.017
it appears at least said, let's move on.

00:09:45.785 --> 00:09:46.919
Partly because look,

00:09:46.919 --> 00:09:49.088
what Prigozhin did here was

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:49.555
will show

00:09:49.555 --> 00:09:50.222
that there is a big

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:51.290
public support

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.758
for how people feel

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:54.060
that the war is being badly

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.328
fought, that you know,

00:09:55.328 --> 00:09:56.228
this has been a big part

00:09:56.228 --> 00:09:57.897
of promotions narrative.

00:09:57.897 --> 00:09:58.464
And he got a lot

00:09:58.464 --> 00:09:59.465
of support on the street.

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:00.967
And that's a very dangerous

